      "side": 1,
      "message": "I apologize, but I still can\u0027t figure out how the code in `testing/helpers/write.cc` is tested currently (i.e. before this CL).\n\nhttps://pdfium-review.googlesource.com/136111 shows that broken `testing/helpers/write.cc` passes CQ even *before* this CL.  We may want to try to improve CQ coverage in a _separate_ CL, but I don\u0027t think the lack of pre-existing coverage should block _this_ CL.\n\n\u003e Since this is about the encoder, you should try to intentionally break `pdfium_test --png`.\n\nHow would I do that?\n\nRunning `out/rust/pdfium_test` just says `No input files` and exits.  Adding a `--png` command-line flag doesn\u0027t change that.\n\nLooking at test logs on the bots, it seems that the \"pixel tests\" step invokes `testing/tools/run_pixel_tests.py` which _already_ ensures that CQ covers passing `--png` flag to `pdfium_test`.  For example, I already see an invocation like this (copied from the log + cleaned-up to use relative paths and avoid python literal syntax):\n\n```\nout/debug_skia_rust_v8/pdfium_test                                \n--send-events                                                     \n--png                                                             \n--md5\n--time\u003d1399672130                                                 \n--font-dir\u003d/b/s/w/ir/cache/builder/pdfium/third_party/test_fonts  \n--croscore-font-names\nout/debug_skia_rust_v8/gen/pdfium/testing/pixel/bug_1258634.pdf\n```\n\n\u003e Every `pdfium_test` call in pixel tests and corpus tests run with `--png` to render to PNG and then compare the output against the baseline.\n\u003e \nAck.  This doesn\u0027t seem to cover the code I am modifying in `testing/helpers/write.cc`.\n\n\u003e See EncodePng() comment in testing/helpers/write.cc.\n\nCan you please provide a code search link?  I searched for \"EncodePng\" in `testing/helpers/write.cc` and there were no comments.",
